---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Play — Azeroth" page="play">
  <section class="page-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="play.eyebrow">JOIN THE REALM</p><h1 data-i18n="play.title">Start playing</h1><p id="home-guide-text" data-i18n="play.intro">Everything you need to enter the realm, from a clean client to your first login.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap play-layout content-section">
    <article class="account-panel play-primary">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="play.installation">INSTALLATION</p><h2 data-i18n="play.stepsTitle">Connect in three steps</h2></div><span class="expansion-pill"><span id="expansion-name">Wrath of the Lich King</span> · <span id="client-version">3.3.5a</span></span></div>
      <ol class="join-checklist">
        <li><b>1</b><div><h3 data-i18n="play.accountTitle">Create your account</h3><p data-i18n="play.accountBody">Your portal login is also your in-game account.</p><a class="text-action" href="/register" data-i18n="play.accountAction">Create account →</a></div></li>
        <li><b>2</b><div><h3>Install a clean client</h3><p>Use client build <strong id="client-build">12340</strong>. Modified clients can cause login or patch errors.</p><a id="download-link" class="button small hidden" rel="noreferrer">Download client</a><p id="download-unavailable" class="notice-inline">No client mirror has been configured yet. Ask staff for the approved download.</p></div></li>
        <li><b>3</b><div><h3 data-i18n="play.realmlistTitle">Set the realmlist</h3><p><span data-i18n="play.realmlistOpen">Open</span> <code>Data/enUS/realmlist.wtf</code> <span data-i18n="play.realmlistInstruction">(or your locale folder) and replace its contents:</span></p><button class="code-copy" data-copy="" data-i18n-aria-label="play.copyRealmlist"><code>set realmlist <i id="realm-address">logon.example.com</i></code><span data-i18n="action.copy">Copy</span></button></div></li>
      </ol>
    </article>
    <aside class="play-sidebar">
      <article class="account-panel"><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU JOIN</p><h2>Realm profile</h2><dl class="compact-definition"><div><dt>Realm</dt><dd data-home-realm>Azeroth</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd id="play-realm-type">PvE</dd></div><div><dt>XP rate</dt><dd id="experience-rate">2×</dd></div><div><dt>Level cap</dt><dd id="play-level-cap">80</dd></div></dl><a class="text-action" href="/realm">Full realm details →</a></article>
      <article id="play-rules" class="account-panel"><p class="eyebrow">RULES</p><h2>Play fair</h2><p id="home-rules">Respect other players, avoid exploits, and follow staff instructions.</p></article>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap content-section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">DOWNLOAD CENTER</p><h2>Official client mirrors</h2></div><p>Verify the checksum before extracting the client.</p></div><div id="download-center" class="download-grid"><p class="muted">Loading configured downloads…</p></div></section>
  <section class="panel-section"><div class="wrap content-section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">PLATFORM NOTES</p><h2>Install safely on your system</h2></div><p>Use only packages and checksums published above.</p></div><div class="faq-grid"><details><summary>Windows</summary><p>Extract the client to a user-writable folder outside Program Files, set the realmlist, and start Wow.exe or the realm's signed launcher.</p></details><details><summary>macOS</summary><p>Use the operator-published macOS package when available. Current macOS versions may require a compatible wrapper; follow the package-specific requirements instead of bypassing platform security.</p></details><details><summary>Linux</summary><p>Run the Windows 3.3.5a client through Wine using a dedicated prefix. Preserve filename casing and configure the realmlist inside the client directory.</p></details><details><summary>Remove or reinstall</summary><p>Back up screenshots and interface settings, then remove the extracted client folder and its launcher data. A clean reinstall should not require system-wide files.</p></details></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap content-section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">TROUBLESHOOTING</p><h2>Common connection problems</h2></div></div><div class="faq-grid"><details><summary>“Unable to connect”</summary><p>Confirm that the realm is online, the realmlist contains only the configured address, and your firewall allows Wow.exe.</p></details><details><summary>Client starts patching</summary><p>Close the launcher and start Wow.exe directly. The supported client is <span id="troubleshooting-client-build">the configured realm build</span>.</p></details><details><summary>Login works on the website only</summary><p>Use your account name—not your email address—in the game client. Account names are case-insensitive.</p></details><details><summary>Still stuck?</summary><p>Sign in and open a support ticket with the exact error message and the steps you already tried.</p><a href="/account">Open account support →</a></details></div></section>
</Layout>
